_entity_id": "7EF7A3"}]}, {"id": "CE43F6207559B52323CEC7E256B8C14D", "headline": "Taiwan Semiconductor Insulated From Short-Term Helium Supply Shock: Analyst", "timestamp": "2026-04-14T12:36:38", "source": {"id": "5A5702", "name": "Benzinga", "rank": "RANK_1"}, "url": "https://www.benzinga.com/node/51801412?utm_campaign=partner_feed&utm_medium=feed&utm_source=ravenpack", "chunks": [{"cnum": 1, "text": "A helium supply crunch tied to escalating tensions in the Middle East is emerging as a new stress point for the global semiconductor industry, raising concerns over chip production even as companies like Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Co. Ltd. (NYSE:TSM) remain well buffered in the near term.\nHighlights Fragile Supply Chains\nEFM Asset Management's Daniel Heyler told CNBC that the helium shortage underscores the complexity of semiconductor supply chains but is manageable in the short term, especially for Taiwan Semiconductor.\nHe said helium demand has surged with advanced EUV chipmaking, but Taiwan Semiconductor is well prepared through recycling and holding roughly three to six months of inventory. As the largest buyer, it is also likely to receive priority supply.", "relevance": 0.4064925056376885, "sentiment": -0.32, "detections": [{"id": "8711ED", "start": 433, "end": 446, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "209994", "start": 317, "end": 330, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "209994", "start": 447, "end": 460, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "9CC31E", "start": 550, "end": 556, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "5E1586", "start": 648, "end": 657, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "9417FE", "start": 204, "end": 258, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "9417FE", "start": 513, "end": 533, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "9417FE", "start": 602, "end": 622, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "3FFDF4", "start": 335, "end": 351, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "ACB6B7", "start": 58, "end": 69, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "9C0E1C", "start": 701, "end": 710, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "7E7529", "start": 170, "end": 180, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "C3A646", "start": 394, "end": 402, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "940A72", "start": 373, "end": 377, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "E2EF93", "start": 119, "end": 141, "type": "entity"}], "text_locations": [{"paragraph_num": 1, "sentence_num": 1}, {"paragraph_num": 2, "sentence_num": 1}, {"paragraph_num": 3, "sentence_num": 1}, {"paragraph_num": 4, "sentence_num": 1}, {"paragraph_num": 4, "sentence_num": 2}], "entity_ids": ["9417FE", "5E1586", "C3A646", "940A72", "8711ED", "3FFDF4", "209994", "ACB6B7", "9CC31E", "7E7529", "9C0E1C", "E2EF93"], "primary_entity_id": "8711ED"}]}, {"id": "BC9C095B32FF8040B60C869629B3DC73", "headline": "Global AI, IT & Telecom Industry Snapshot", "timestamp": "2026-04-14T12:47:52", "source": {"id": "6664EC", "name": "FRPT Informedia Services", "rank": "RANK_1"}, "url": "https://research.bluematrix.com/docs/pdf/6d92150e-fa8b-4b26-9540-244aa482df34/0e64ad30-da6f-44f7-8c11-f5be7c47c7e5", "chunks": [{"cnum": 11, "text": "Rampant Al demand for memory is fueling a growing chip crisis\nA growing procession of tech industry leaders including Elon Musk and Tim Cook are warning about a global crisis in the making: A shortage of memory chips is beginning to hammer profits, derail corporate plans and inflate price tags on everything from laptops and smartphones to automobiles and data centers - and the crunch is only going to get worse. Since the start of 2026, Tesla Inc., Apple Inc. and a dozen other major corporations have signaled that the shortage of DRAM, or dynamic random access memory - the fundamental building block of almost all technology - will constrain production. Cook warned it will compress iPhone margins. Micron Technology Inc. called the bottleneck \"unprecedented.\" Musk got to the intractable nature of the problem when he declared Tesla is going to have to build its own memory fabrication plant.\nHapser Data Services\n8\n[Hapser Data Services logo]", "relevance": 0.35959210093250743, "sentiment": -0.83, "detections": [{"id": "CE464B", "start": 118, "end": 127, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "CE464B", "start": 767, "end": 771, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "277B39", "start": 284, "end": 289, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "60E849", "start": 314, "end": 321, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "3F335B", "start": 204, "end": 216, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "FA1880", "start": 357, "end": 369, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "CC71F7", "start": 907, "end": 911, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "CC71F7", "start": 931, "end": 935, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "7E7529", "start": 648, "end": 658, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "5C3ECD", "start": 86, "end": 99, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "5C3ECD", "start": 620, "end": 630, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "9CC31E", "start": 11, "end": 17, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "D8442A", "start": 452, "end": 462, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "7373D4", "start": 689, "end": 695, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "E4AFAD", "start": 341, "end": 352, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "14DCC5", "start": 50, "end": 54, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "253C3A", "start": 240, "end": 247, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "E7C37B", "start": 341, "end": 352, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "DD3BB1", "start": 440, "end": 450, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "DD3BB1", "start": 834, "end": 839, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "6BD43B", "start": 132, "end": 140, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "6BD43B", "start": 660, "end": 664, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "0BB855", "start": 326, "end": 337, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "C3A646", "start": 192, "end": 200, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "C3A646", "start": 523, "end": 531, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "49BBBC", "start": 705, "end": 727, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "F3F199", "start": 535, "end": 539, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "F3F199", "start": 544, "end": 572, "type": "entity"}], "locations": [{"page": 8, "bottom": 0.478, "left": 0.142, "right": 0.73, "top": 0.463}, {"page": 8, "bottom": 0.846, "left": 0.142, "right": 0.847, "top": 0.495}, {"page": 8, "bottom": 0.911, "left": 0.15, "right": 0.31, "top": 0.897}, {"page": 8, "bottom": 0.911, "left": 0.794, "right": 0.804, "top": 0.897}, {"page": 9, "bottom": 0.137, "left": 0.142, "right": 0.35, "top": 0.108}], "text_locations": [{"paragraph_num": 67, "sentence_num": 1}, {"paragraph_num": 68, "sentence_num": 1}, {"paragraph_num": 68, "sentence_num": 2}, {"paragraph_num": 68, "sentence_num": 3}, {"paragraph_num": 68, "sentence_num": 4}, {"paragraph_num": 68, "sentence_num": 5}, {"paragraph_num": 69, "sentence_num": 1}, {"paragraph_num": 70, "sentence_num": 1}, {"paragraph_num": 71, "sentence_num": 1}], "entity_ids": ["14DCC5", "F3F199", "7E7529", "C3A646", "DD3BB1", "CE464B", "E7C37B", "6BD43B", "60E849", "7373D4", "FA1880", "D8442A", "9CC31E", "277B39", "49BBBC", "3F335B", "5C3ECD", "0BB855", "CC71F7", "253C3A", "E4AFAD"], "primary_entity_id": "CE464B"}]}, {"id": "D15322E8E9537FA7E6EB9EF8B16AF250", "headline": "1 Reason Why April 10 Could Be Huge for Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing", "timestamp": "2026-04-03T11:02:18", "source": {"id": "7DFD4A", "name": "Nasdaq", "rank": "RANK_2"}, "url": "https://www.nasdaq.com/articles/1-reason-why-april-10-could-be-huge-taiwan-semiconductor-manufacturing", "chunks": [{"cnum": 3, "text": "Broadcom has flagged that capacity constraints at TSMC are emerging as a key bottleneck in the AI supply chain. As demand for advanced chips continues to surge, limited foundry capacity is increasingly restricting how quickly that demand can be fulfilled.\nAt the same time, geopolitical risks have also soared. The ongoing Iran conflict has disrupted global energy flows, particularly through the Strait of Hormuz, which handles roughly 20% of global oil and liquified natural gas (LNG) shipments. With Taiwan importing almost 95% of its energy needs and natural gas accounting for nearly 48% of the island's electricity generation, semiconductor production at TSMC is exposed to the risk of fuel supply disruptions in Taiwan. The shortage of helium, which is required for chip manufacturing, is further aggravating the supply problem.", "relevance": 0.3382734319933956, "sentiment": -0.74, "detections": [{"id": "9CC31E", "start": 115, "end": 121, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "9CC31E", "start": 231, "end": 237, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "BFD8F6", "start": 274, "end": 292, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "AE4E73", "start": 323, "end": 327, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "09DE1F", "start": 0, "end": 8, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "7EF7A3", "start": 567, "end": 577, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "8801A6", "start": 510, "end": 519, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "0D59A1", "start": 397, "end": 413, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "EEFB41", "start": 609, "end": 631, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "42470E", "start": 459, "end": 480, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "42470E", "start": 482, "end": 485, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "42470E", "start": 555, "end": 566, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "C3A646", "start": 731, "end": 739, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "38918B", "start": 91, "end": 97, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "9417FE", "start": 50, "end": 54, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "9417FE", "start": 661, "end": 665, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "1C69E3", "start": 358, "end": 364, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "1C69E3", "start": 538, "end": 544, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "884897", "start": 503, "end": 509, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "884897", "start": 719, "end": 725, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "F20FAB", "start": 35, "end": 46, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "209994", "start": 98, "end": 110, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "7E7529", "start": 647, "end": 657, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "FD9CFE", "start": 451, "end": 454, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "8711ED", "start": 633, "end": 646, "type": "entity"}], "text_locations": [{"paragraph_num": 12, "sentence_num": 1}, {"paragraph_num": 12, "sentence_num": 2}, {"paragraph_num": 13, "sentence_num": 1}, {"paragraph_num": 13, "sentence_num": 2}, {"paragraph_num": 13, "sentence_num": 3}, {"paragraph_num": 13, "sentence_num": 4}], "entity_ids": ["9417FE", "AE4E73", "884897", "7E7529", "09DE1F", "C3A646", "F20FAB", "EEFB41", "8801A6", "42470E", "38918B", "1C69E3", "9CC31E", "FD9CFE", "8711ED", "0D59A1", "209994", "7EF7A3", "BFD8F6"], "primary_entity_id": "9CC31E"}]}, {"id": "0BD5171468B02019B1889C6A8BEADB98", "headline": "ChipMOS TECHNOLOGIES INC: Q4 2025 Earnings Call on Apr 14, 2026 - Report", "timestamp": "2026-04-14T12:00:00", "source": {"id": "28DED6", "name": "Quartr Reports", "rank": "RANK_1"}, "url": "https://files.quartr.com/reports/10c40c0bbd51ff44a74cc511954dc0b9-2026-08-11-09-48-30.pdf?ref=UmF2ZW5QYWNr", "chunks": [{"cnum": 97, "text": "The Semiconductor Industry and Conditions of Outsourcing in Taiwan and Mainland China\nTaiwan is one of the world's leading locations for outsourced semiconductor manufacturing. The semiconductor industry supply chain in Taiwan has developed such that the various stages of the semiconductor manufacturing process have been disaggregated, thus allowing for specialization. The disaggregation of the semiconductor manufacturing process in Taiwan permits these semiconductor manufacturing service providers to focus on particular parts of the production process, develop economies of scale, maintain higher capacity utilization rates and remain flexible in responding to customer needs by lowering time-to-market pressure faced by semiconductor companies. There are several leading service providers in Taiwan, each of which offers substantial capacity, high-quality manufacturing, leading semiconductor wafer fabrication, test, assembly and process technologies, and a full range of services. These service providers have access to an educated labor pool and a large number of engineers suitable for sophisticated manufacturing industries. As a result, many of the world's leading semiconductor companies outsource some or all of their semiconductor manufacturing needs to Taiwan's semiconductor manufacturing service providers and take advantage of the close proximity among facilities in the supply chain. In addition, companies located in Taiwan are very active in the design and manufacture of electronic systems, which has created significant local demand for semiconductor devices.", "relevance": 0.2950960329161971, "sentiment": -0.27, "detections": [{"id": "E2EF93", "start": 4, "end": 26, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "E2EF93", "start": 181, "end": 203, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "FDA972", "start": 568, "end": 586, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "75A2FF", "start": 668, "end": 682, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "7E7529", "start": 540, "end": 550, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "C254A4", "start": 45, "end": 56, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "4C6558", "start": 604, "end": 630, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "5442E4", "start": 1126, "end": 1136, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "FB4F3F", "start": 1496, "end": 1514, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "729D37", "start": 901, "end": 906, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "9CC31E", "start": 1552, "end": 1558, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "8711ED", "start": 148, "end": 161, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "8711ED", "start": 277, "end": 290, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "8711ED", "start": 398, "end": 411, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "8711ED", "start": 458, "end": 471, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "8711ED", "start": 728, "end": 741, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "8711ED", "start": 887, "end": 900, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "8711ED", "start": 1179, "end": 1192, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "8711ED", "start": 1234, "end": 1247, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "8711ED", "start": 1563, "end": 1576, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "209994", "start": 204, "end": 216, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "209994", "start": 1392, "end": 1404, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "F26C2F", "start": 947, "end": 959, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "441EAE", "start": 1042, "end": 1052, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "75A8CD", "start": 162, "end": 175, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "75A8CD", "start": 291, "end": 312, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "75A8CD", "start": 412, "end": 433, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "75A8CD", "start": 472, "end": 485, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "75A8CD", "start": 864, "end": 877, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "75A8CD", "start": 1112, "end": 1125, "