 6% year-over-year as Dynamic Random Access Memory (DRAM) and Not AND (NAND) shortages disrupted supply and raised costs across manufacturers.\nJain noted that memory suppliers prioritized AI data centers over consumer electronics, forcing OEMs to absorb higher bills of materials or pass costs to consumers.\nShe added that rising energy prices, logistics costs, and geopolitical tensions weakened consumer sentiment, particularly impacting entry- and mid-range segments.\nApple Leads While Samsung Faces Delays\nApple captured the top spot with a 21% market share and 5% growth, supported by strong demand for the iPhone 17, supply chain execution, and resilience in premium segments.", "relevance": 0.2920917055357904, "sentiment": -0.47, "detections": [{"id": "53793B", "start": 708, "end": 718, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "23E2A4", "start": 172, "end": 177, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "23E2A4", "start": 345, "end": 350, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "23E2A4", "start": 412, "end": 417, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "46E936", "start": 606, "end": 618, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "B811D5", "start": 546, "end": 553, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "913660", "start": 354, "end": 363, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "913660", "start": 454, "end": 462, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "277B39", "start": 394, "end": 400, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "C590B1", "start": 154, "end": 160, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "2C3A26", "start": 669, "end": 678, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "209994", "start": 680, "end": 692, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "F3F199", "start": 79, "end": 107, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "F3F199", "start": 109, "end": 113, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "C6DF77", "start": 233, "end": 244, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "FA1880", "start": 248, "end": 260, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "9CCADF", "start": 402, "end": 411, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "D8442A", "start": 528, "end": 533, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "D8442A", "start": 567, "end": 572, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "C3A646", "start": 134, "end": 143, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "1C69E3", "start": 387, "end": 393, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "9CC31E", "start": 654, "end": 660, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "0BB855", "start": 32, "end": 42, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "C5607F", "start": 223, "end": 232, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "1C1527", "start": 266, "end": 286, "type": "entity"}], "text_locations": [{"paragraph_num": 6, "sentence_num": 1}, {"paragraph_num": 7, "sentence_num": 1}, {"paragraph_num": 8, "sentence_num": 1}, {"paragraph_num": 9, "sentence_num": 1}, {"paragraph_num": 10, "sentence_num": 1}], "entity_ids": ["23E2A4", "2C3A26", "C6DF77", "53793B", "46E936", "F3F199", "1C1527", "C3A646", "C5607F", "FA1880", "D8442A", "913660", "1C69E3", "9CC31E", "277B39", "0BB855", "B811D5", "209994", "C590B1", "9CCADF"], "primary_entity_id": "53793B"}]}, {"id": "945A9C4AA2D282710FDAE0716C0A169F", "headline": "Intel Wins Google Promise to Keep Using Xeon in Data Centers", "timestamp": "2026-04-09T20:17:56", "source": {"id": "UBE8KM", "name": "Bloomberg Businessweek", "rank": "RANK_1"}, "url": "https://podtrac.com/pts/redirect.mp3/tracking.swap.fm/track/UVBrz8bN8aM2Xe47PEPu/tracking.swap.fm/track/UVBrz8bN8aM2Xe47PEPu/traffic.omny.fm/d/clips/e73c998e-6e60-432f-8610-ae210140c5b1/3b082bbf-691d-443b-bc59-ae2b0012ff93/2a43ce9e-90cb-4d21-98b4-b427014c7300/audio.mp3?utm_source=Podcast&in_playlist=9222076a-d22a-4a9f-9d26-ae2b0012ffb4", "chunks": [{"cnum": 7, "text": "Well you know Ian one of the questions we've been having a lot is you know there's everybody's been talking about the duration of this war and the impact on everything in our world and it determines the economic outlooks for the US globally but you know supply chains what happens longer term but I am also thinking about once again these wars these incidents Just like the pandemic reminds us of these global supply chains and where there are concentrations around the world and I always think about TSMC right in Taiwan and just you know that over exposure if you will. Are we seeing global supply chains for semiconductors being more spread out? Can they spread out even more? Well as you know there's been a significant attempt to relocate or to recreate the chip industry in the United States but You know going back to helium this helium that we're talking about shortages of effects TSMC effects Taiwan and effects South Korea and those two areas absolute concentrations of essential chip making Whether it's memory or whether it's made toward a production of high-end AI semiconductors. So this isn't good.", "relevance": 0.2855492964787441, "sentiment": -0.61, "detections": [{"id": "B47C69", "start": 135, "end": 138, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "B47C69", "start": 339, "end": 343, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "38918B", "start": 1076, "end": 1078, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "5442E4", "start": 768, "end": 776, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "25B4E2", "start": 922, "end": 933, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "C3A646", "start": 869, "end": 878, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "471AC1", "start": 374, "end": 382, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "8711ED", "start": 611, "end": 625, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "8711ED", "start": 1079, "end": 1093, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "3D4567", "start": 229, "end": 231, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "3D4567", "start": 780, "end": 797, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "884897", "start": 515, "end": 521, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "884897", "start": 903, "end": 909, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "7E7529", "start": 1053, "end": 1063, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "209994", "start": 254, "end": 267, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "209994", "start": 410, "end": 423, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "209994", "start": 593, "end": 606, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "9417FE", "start": 501, "end": 505, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "9417FE", "start": 890, "end": 894, "type": "entity"}], "text_locations": [{"paragraph_num": 10, "sentence_num": 1}, {"paragraph_num": 10, "sentence_num": 2}, {"paragraph_num": 10, "sentence_num": 3}, {"paragraph_num": 10, "sentence_num": 4}, {"paragraph_num": 10, "sentence_num": 5}], "entity_ids": ["9417FE", "38918B", "5442E4", "3D4567", "C3A646", "8711ED", "209994", "25B4E2", "471AC1", "884897", "7E7529", "B47C69"], "primary_entity_id": "B47C69"}]}, {"id": "D91C2E24E69268C1868ACE8DF8BB383D", "headline": "1 Reason Why April 10 Could Be Huge for Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing", "timestamp": "2026-04-03T10:38:03", "source": {"id": "0A7563", "name": "The Globe And Mail", "rank": "RANK_1"}, "url": "https://www.theglobeandmail.com/investing/markets/markets-news/Motley%20Fool/1132068/1-reason-why-april-10-could-be-huge-for-taiwan-semiconductor-manufacturing/", "chunks": [{"cnum": 1, "text": "Key Points\nSupply constraints and geopolitical risks are emerging as key risks for semiconductor stocks.\nTSMC has become a critical bottleneck in the artificial intelligence (AI) chip supply chain.\nEnergy disruptions and helium shortages can limit how much AI demand TSMC can actually fulfill.\nSemiconductor stocks are no longer driven solely by artificial intelligence (AI) demand. Instead, supply constraints and geopolitical risk are becoming increasingly important in the current market environment.\nTaiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing (NYSE: TSM) , the leading chip manufacturer with a 72% share of the global foundry market, will report its March 2026 sales on April 10. That data point will provide investors with a real-time indication of how much AI demand the company is managing to actually fulfill amid the ongoing Iran conflict.", "relevance": 0.26926708313717046, "sentiment": -0.37, "detections": [{"id": "D93711", "start": 11, "end": 29, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "D93711", "start": 392, "end": 410, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "C3A646", "start": 228, "end": 237, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "AE4E73", "start": 826, "end": 830, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "9417FE", "start": 105, "end": 109, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "9417FE", "start": 267, "end": 271, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "9417FE", "start": 504, "end": 550, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "9417FE", "start": 765, "end": 776, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "9CC31E", "start": 260, "end": 266, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "9CC31E", "start": 375, "end": 381, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "9CC31E", "start": 758, "end": 764, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "C4F920", "start": 97, "end": 103, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "C4F920", "start": 308, "end": 314, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "C4F920", "start": 594, "end": 599, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "00DBA0", "start": 150, "end": 183, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "8711ED", "start": 83, "end": 96, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "8711ED", "start": 294, "end": 307, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "BFD8F6", "start": 34, "end": 52, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "BFD8F6", "start": 415, "end": 432, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "1C69E3", "start": 198, "end": 204, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "EF59C7", "start": 484, "end": 502, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "209994", "start": 184, "end": 196, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "CC71F7", "start": 681, "end": 685, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "38918B", "start": 257, "end": 259, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "38918B", "start": 346, "end": 374, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "38918B", "start": 755, "end": 757, "type": "entity"}], "text_locations": [{"paragraph_num": 1, "sentence_num": 1}, {"paragraph_num": 2, "sentence_num": 1}, {"paragraph_num": 3, "sentence_num": 1}, {"paragraph_num": 4, "sentence_num": 1}, {"paragraph_num": 5, "sentence_num": 1}, {"paragraph_num": 5, "sentence_num": 2}, {"paragraph_num": 6, "sentence_num": 1}, {"paragraph_num": 6, "sentence_num": 2}], "entity_ids": ["9417FE", "D93711", "38918B", "C3A646", "EF59C7", "8711ED", "1C69E3", "CC71F7", "209994", "AE4E73", "9CC31E", "C4F920", "BFD8F6", "00DBA0"], "primary_entity_id": "D93711"}]}, {"id": "E4CDD8B125CE3C68C95DF82E15C3A9B9", "headline": "Semiconductors - The semiconductor is not to blame", "timestamp": "2026-04-03T16:24:08", "source": {"id": "114A6B", "name": "KTB Investment & Securities Co., Ltd", "rank": "RANK_1"}, "url": "https://research.bluematrix.com/docs/pdf/ddca69d6-27c0-4d76-9404-14ae9474ae93/8f1e48cf-e11e-4fb1-a2c3-db548e5947e5", "chunks": [{"cnum": 19, "text": "Meta\n- Securing sufficient infrastructure capacity in 2026 is key\n- Power infrastructure for the Louisiana data center will be expanded by 5.2GW to over 7GW in total\n- Pursuing AI data center investments in the hundreds of billions of dollars\nOpenAl\n- Expanded computing power by 9.5 times from 0.2GW in 2023 to 1.9GW in 2025\n- If more computing resources were available, customer adoption and monetization would have been much faster\n- Aiming to secure 10GW of data center CAPA across the United States\n- Even assuming maximum chip production from current suppliers, there is still a shortage\nTesla\n- Even assuming maximum chip production from suppliers, there is a shortage\n- Aiming to secure 1TW of compute capacity annually\n- Tesla will need a 'Tera(TW)fab' far larger than GW-scale fab\nTSMC\n- TSMC's production capacity has reached its limit. Foundry CAPA constraints lead to AI chip shortages\n- The explosive growth in token usage leads to increased demand for advanced silicon\n- Amidst the AI megatrend, semiconductor demand will remain very robust\nNVIDIA\n- Need to build GW-scale AI super factories by connecting data centers\nSource: Various companies, Media compilation, Daol Investment & Securities", "relevance": 0.26349819935302304, "sentiment": -0.44, "detections": [{"id": "14DCC5", "start": 528, "end": 532, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "14DCC5", "start": 624, "end": 628, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "7E7529", "start": 533, "end": 543, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "7E7529", "start": 629, "end": 639, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "FE1757", "start": 235, "end": 242, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "DD3BB1", "start": 594, "end": 599, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "DD3BB1", "start": 730, "end": 735, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "9417FE", "start": 791, "end": 795, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "9417FE", "start": 798, "end": 802, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "12E454", "start": 0, "end": 4, "type": "entity"}, {"id": "8A982